{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>היתה</b> — Some say: it is his thirst and his tears, which are [like] water, as in 'לחם לו' (his bread). The meaning of the weeping: because of the length of the exile, and he does not go up on pilgrimage to rejoice. And some say: that he weeps and sheds tears [as constantly as] his food. [n: The comparison 'כמו מאכלו' is elliptical; translated hyper-literally. The reading 'הוא צמא ודמעיו' is itself difficult as the subject of היתה.]" "<b>יומם ולילה</b> — continually, in secret and in public." "And the meaning of 'Where is your Elohim' — that you used to go up three times a year to see His face."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:34.294324719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}